     "headerLink": "",
     "type": "mask_imgtext",
     "title": "",
     "text": "<p>In winter, the mountain draws nearer. When snow settles like a protective blanket across the slopes, lines become clearer. What holds, remains. What does not, steps back. In the first light of day, the crunch of tracks breaks the softened quiet - long before the first gondola reaches the mountain. Nature sets the rhythm: crisp air, low sounds, warmth by the fire. From stillness grows a sense of shelter; time loses its urgency here. Unvarnished and unfiltered, winter turns the gaze toward what holds: the simple. The real.&nbsp;</p>",
